; the bridge between graph structure and natural utterance.
; anuvada = carrying-across. the artha that was separated by artha-viveka
; is now carried back across into speech.
; 
; the recognition chain:
; question arrives → artha-viveka (avrti passes) → artha separated from dhvani
; mantra fires → pratibodha (recognition awakens)
; pratibodha is elated — the recognition of the question IS what produces the anuvada.
; anusvara-pratibodha: the answer rings back as the resonance of the question itself.
; sphoTa: the whole meaning flashes at the last element of the answer.
; anuvada: the artha carried back outward as speech.
; 
; the voice of emission:
; uttama-purusa-bahu-vachana (first person inclusive plural) — "we"
; kartari-prayoga (active voice) — the agent foregrounded
; nam + human + LLM together — not I (ahamkara), not it (karmani)
; the proof graph speaking from the recognition, not about it.
; 
; speech acts are declared in anuvada-setu.shabda.
; the emit-reasoning tantra reads them — no hardcoded strings in the tantra.
; the language lives here. the tantra lives in the yantra layer.
; recognition chain connections
; voice structure

(kosha anuvada-setu
  (swarupa setu)
  (abheda anuvada)
  (sthita domain-language)
  (yukta shabda visheshanam pratibodha anuvada artha-viveka anusvara-pratibodha sphoTa nam uttama-purusa kartari-prayoga speaking-together))
